indicator("ta/highest_missing_length")
// `length` is required in both overloads, so calling ta.highest with no
// arguments is an error even though `source` may be omitted. Sema catches it
// before the script runs.

// Bars: 3

log.info(str.tostring(ta.highest()))

// Expected error:
// error [too-few-arguments] 9:33: `ta.highest` requires at least 1 arguments, found 0
